---
description: IPTV comprehensive validation protocol
globs: ["**/*.m3u", "**/*.m3u8", "**/darkcdn.store", "scripts/iptv-*.cjs"]
---

When validating IPTV files, ALWAYS:

1. Check structural integrity (#EXTM3U header, #EXTINF tags, valid URLs)
2. Perform HTTP health checks on all stream URLs (expect 200–299)
3. Validate HLS manifests (segment URIs reachable)
4. Test darkcdn.store endpoints for CDN availability and response time
5. Run ffprobe on a sample of streams for H.264/AAC codec support
6. Flag geo-restrictions (403, suspicious redirects)
7. Detect duplicate channel names across playlists
8. Verify EPG URL references (url-tvg, xmltv.php)
9. Generate a Markdown report under `reports/iptv-audit/`
10. Append timestamps to `.cursor/iptv-test.log`

Run the full suite with:

```bash
node scripts/iptv-comprehensive-audit.cjs
```

For playlist-only scheduled checks:

```bash
node scripts/iptv-playlist-health-check.cjs --playlist "$IPTV_HEALTH_PLAYLIST"
```
